#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""kvpn — headless connect to the KAIST VPN (Ivanti Connect Secure + AirCUVE 2Auth).

Does the whole login in the terminal — id/password, SMS or Email code entry —
then brings the tunnel up via openconnect. No browser required.

Flow (reverse-engineered from the live service):
  1. GET  kvpn.kaist.ac.kr/            -> Ivanti sign-in session (DSSIGNIN)
  2. GET  portal /view/redirectVPN     -> portal session (JSESSIONID) + correlation code
  3. POST login.cgi (user+pass+realm+handshake) -> validate primary credentials
     GET  portal /view/onepassCheck (code suffix only) -> /vpnInit
     GET  portal /oauth/authorize -> /request; POST /view/redirect -> OTP menu
  4. POST portal /api/portal           -> send SMS/Email code
  5. POST portal /j_spring_security_check.do -> verify code (-> OAuth)
  6. GET  portal /vpn/<client_id>?code -> read `message` = the password#2 token
  7. POST login.cgi (user+pass+realm+password#2) -> DSID
  8. openconnect --protocol=nc --cookie-on-stdin kvpn.kaist.ac.kr

Credentials can optionally be stored (password in the macOS Keychain or Windows
Credential Manager, id/realm in the platform config directory); `kvpn --forget`
removes them again.

Requires: Python 3 (stdlib only) and OpenConnect.
"""
